{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Forty years old.</b> For when Abraham came back from Mount Moriah, he was told that Rebekah had been born, and Isaac was thirty-seven years old — for in that very passage Sarah died, and from Isaac's birth until the Akedah when Sarah died was thirty-seven years: for she was ninety when Isaac was born, and one hundred twenty-seven when she died — as it says, ״וַיִּהְיוּ חַיֵּי שָׂרָה״ and so on. So Isaac was thirty-seven years old, and in that very passage Rebekah was born. He waited for her until she was fit for relations three years and married her." "<b>The daughter of Bethuel of Paddan-aram, the sister of Laban.</b> But was it not already written that she was the daughter of Bethuel and sister of Laban and from Paddan-aram? Rather, to tell her praise — that she was the daughter of a wicked man and sister of a wicked man and her place was men of wickedness, yet she did not learn from their deeds." "<b>Of Paddan-aram.</b> Because there were two Arams — Aram-naharaim and Aram-zobah — he calls it Paddan, a term for a pair of cattle; the Targum renders פַּדַּן as תּוֹרִין. And some interpret פַּדַּן אֲרָם as שְׂדֵה אֲרָם, for in the Ishmaelite language they call a field פַּדַּן."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:29.462736874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}